# The model library itself is ~18 GB of vendor STLs and slicer projects.
# Only the tracker, its reference data and its generated dashboard are versioned.
*.stl
*.lys
*.ctp
*.chitubox
# Sliced output. These never used to appear in the repo — they lived on the
# printer — so nothing caught that they were unignored until the rotY sweep
# dropped 62 MB files into sweeps/. The analysis under forensics/ is what we
# keep, not the slice.
*.goo
*.ctb
*.pdf
*.jpg
# The vendor's .webp/.avif logo renders are deliberately NOT ignored: GitHub
# Pages needs them in the repo to show the dashboard to Brian, and the webp is
# 1000x1000 at ~11 KB, smaller than the ignored Release_*.jpg photos.
*.png
# ...but keep the cached build-plate previews: the .goo they come from is
# eventually deleted off the printer, so these become the only record of
# what a plate held.
!plates/
!plates/*.png
# Gallery photographs are the record of finished work and Pages must serve
# them, so they are committed too.
!gallery/
!gallery/*
# Forensic analyses: ~125 KB per print, and the whole point is that they
# outlive the 100-360 MB slicer file they came from.
!forensics/
!forensics/**
*_autosave/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.log

# UVtools ships as a 267 MB linux-x64 bundle; it is a tool we run, not
# something this repo should carry.
uvtools/
_to_delete/
